no ACCESS_LEVEL, no MAJOR_USE_DESC; joins via SPACE_UNIT_KEY.\n- ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD: has access level and floor but \"without the area and use-key columns carried by FCLT_ROOMS.\"\n→ Only FCLT_ROOMS carries all four required room attributes (AREA, ACCESS_LEVEL, MAJOR_USE_DESC, ORGANIZATION_NAME, FLOOR) plus the FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY join path.\n\n**3b. Major-use-description source:** FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC vs FCLT_MAJOR_USE.DESCRIPTION.\n- FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC: denormalized, \"e.g. classroom\"; used directly in precedents dw_4776/dw_3299/dw_3332/dw_4590.\n- FCLT_MAJOR_USE.DESCRIPTION: lookup value \"e.g. 'CLASSROOMS'\"; used in dw_3890 via join.\n→ The question says \"major use description\" without referencing the lookup table; FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC is the direct match and avoids an extra join.\n\n**3c. Supervisor-usage join path:** direct (FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY = SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES) vs via SPACE_UNIT.\n- Direct: one join, no fan-out risk from multiple space units per DLC.\n- Via SPACE_UNIT: needed only when space-unit attributes (name/code) are requested; can fan out if multiple space units share a DLC_KEY.\n→ This question does not reference space units; the direct path is cleaner and matches the documented \"DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY\" join.\n\n**3d. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:**\n\n| Requirement | FCLT_ROOMS | FCLT_ORGANIZATION | SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| major use description (group key) | SUPPORTED (MAJOR_USE_DESC) | — | — |\n| organization name (group key) | SUPPORTED (ORGANIZATION_NAME) | SUPPORTED (ORGANIZATION_NAME) | — |\n| room area > 100 filter | SUPPORTED (AREA) | — | — |\n| access level = 1 filter | SUPPORTED (ACCESS_LEVEL) | — | — |\n| number of rooms (COUNT) | SUPPORTED (row grain = one room) | — | — |\n| minimum floor number | SUPPORTED (FLOOR) | — | — |\n| geometric mean of supervisees (>0) | — | — | SUPPORTED (NUM_OF_SUPERVISEES) |\n| total research volume (>0) | — | — | SUPPORTED (RESEARCH_VOLUME) |\n| join room→org | — | SUPPORTED (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) | — |\n| join org→supervisor | — | SUPPORTED (DLC_KEY) | SUPPORTED (DEPT_NAMES) |\n\n**3e. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"major use description\" → FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC (column desc literally \"Major use description\").\n- \"organization name\" → FCLT_ROOMS.ORGANIZATION_NAME (column desc \"Organization name occupying the room\").\n- \"room area is greater than 100\" → FCLT_ROOMS.AREA > 100 (column desc \"Room area in square meters\").\n- \"access level is 1\" → FCLT_ROOMS.ACCESS_LEVEL = 1 (column_concept_access_level confirms room-level ACCESS_LEVEL in FCLT_ROOMS; column desc explicitly gives \"e.g. ACCESS_LEVEL = 1\").\n- \"number of rooms\" → COUNT(*) over FCLT_ROOMS rows (granularity \"one row per room\").\n- \"minimum floor number\" → MIN(FCLT_ROOMS.FLOOR).\n- \"number of supervisees for each department\" → SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.NUM_OF_SUPERVISEES, where DEPT_NAMES is the department DLC key.\n- \"research volume for each organization\" → SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.RESEARCH_VOLUME, attributed to the organization via the DLC_KEY join.\n\n**3f. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- Geometric-mean idiom `EXP(AVG(LN(x)))` with `x > 0` in WHERE: 2 precedents (dw_4061, dw_4701).\n- SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE joined via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY: 3 precedents (dw_2896, dw_4612, dw_4452).\n- FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC / ORGANIZATION_NAME used directly: 4 precedents (dw_4776, dw_3299, dw_3332, dw_4590).\n- FCLT_ROOMS → FCLT_ORGANIZATION via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY: 3 precedents (dw_3410, dw_1465, dw_1833).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- FCLT_ROOMS is the canonical room inventory for facilities/space analysis; consumed by metrics involving room area statistics, access-level filtering, major-use grouping, and organization attribution.\n- FCLT_ORGANIZATION is the organization dimension bridging rooms (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) to DLC keys (via DLC_KEY), enabling cross-domain joins to supervisor usage, HR org units, and department hierarchies.\n- SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE is consumed by 3 metrics (dw_2896, dw_4612, dw_4452), all joining via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY to attribute supervisee counts and research volumes to departments/organizations.\n- The geometric-mean idiom EXP(AVG(LN(x))) is established in dw_4061 and dw_4701 for \"geometric mean of X where X > 0\" question shapes.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n| Entity | Tools called |\n|---|---|\n| FCLT_ROOMS | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph (query_neighbors) |\n| FCLT_ORGANIZATION | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph (metrics_by_table) |\n| SPACE_UNIT | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| FCLT_MAJOR_USE | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_4061 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_4701 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_2896 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_4612 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_4452 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_4776 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_3890 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_3410 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_1465 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_1833 | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| dw_1212, dw_3644 | semantic_get |\n| column_concept_access_level | semantic_search |\n| concept_room_space_inventory | semantic_search |\n| concept_facility_organization_dimension | semantic_search |\n| column_concept_dlc_key | semantic_search |\n\nAll Phase-1 entities were investigated. mysql_query could not be executed due to a persistent authentication error (6 attempts, all returning `Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost' (using password: YES)`).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Recommended tables/columns:**\n- **FCLT_ROOMS** (`r`): measure/filter source — `AREA > 100`, `ACCESS_LEVEL = 1`, `MAJOR_USE_DESC` (group key), `ORGANIZATION_NAME` (group key), `FLOOR` (MIN), row count (COUNT(*)), `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (join key).\n- **FCLT_ORGANIZATION** (`o`): bridge — `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (join to rooms), `DLC_KEY` (join to supervisor usage).\n- **SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE** (`s`): measure source — `DEPT_NAMES` (join key = o.DLC_KEY), `NUM_OF_SUPERVISEES` (geometric mean, filter > 0), `RESEARCH_VOLUME` (SUM, filter > 0).\n\n**6b. Recommended SQL writing approach:**\n- Join path: `FCLT_ROOMS r JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION o ON r.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY = o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY JOIN SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE s ON o.DLC_KEY = s.DEPT_NAMES`.\n- Filters in WHERE: `r.AREA > 100 AND r.ACCESS_LEVEL = 1 AND s.NUM_OF_SUPERVISEES > 0 AND s.RESEARCH_VOLUME > 0` (following the dw_4061 precedent of placing \"> 0\" conditions in WHERE).\n- Aggregation: `GROUP BY r.MAJOR_USE_DESC, r.ORGANIZATION_NAME`.\n- Measures: `COUNT(*)`, `MIN(r.FLOOR)`, `EXP(AVG(LN(s.NUM_OF_SUPERVISEES)))`, `SUM(s.RESEARCH_VOLUME)`.\n- Caveats: NUM_OF_SUPERVISEES observed range is 1-121, so the `> 0` filter is effectively a no-op but is included for literal fidelity to the question. RESEARCH_VOLUME \"can be negative,\" so the `> 0` filter is material. The join `o.DLC_KEY = s.DEPT_NAMES` only matches single-department supervisor rows (documented). No fan-out risk from SPACE_UNIT since it is not in the path.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data perspective**: FCLT_ROOMS is the only room table carrying all required attributes (AREA, ACCESS_LEVEL, MAJOR_USE_DESC, ORGANIZATION_NAME, FLOOR) plus FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY (column definitions retrieved via semantic_get). FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY and SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES share the DLC-key value domain (documented join). NUM_OF_SUPERVISEES range 1-121 ensures LN() is defined. RESEARCH_VOLUME can be negative, so the > 0 filter prevents LN-domain issues for the sum (though SUM doesn't need LN, the filter is semantically required by the question).\n- **Semantic-network perspective**: semantic_graph confirms FCLT_ROOMS→FCLT_ORGANIZATION join edge; SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE table desc documents \"DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY\" join to \"other DLC